--
Per [expr.new]/24 and [expr.delete]/6: `new T[N]` runs T's default
constructor N times, and `delete[] ptr` runs T's destructor N times.

Previously CBMC's `cpp_new_initializer` and `convert_cpp_delete` each
contained a "build loop" placeholder that did nothing.  This test
verifies the implementations now match the standard.
